  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="85ff-922d-493e-b1a4" name="Early Imperial Roman - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>Early Imperial Roman (30 BC to 193 AD)

This list takes the army from the triumph of Augustus to the time of Septimius Severus. The backbone of the army in this period is the legionary infantry, but its supports have become more regular and the cavalry is much improved. Apart from the civil war of 69AD the Roman state was largely stable during this period. Imperial expansion continued for over a hundred years, the last conquest being that of Dacia by Trajan.

ARMY COMPOSITION (as printed in AoA2):
[Early Army 30 BC to 110 AD]
  Characters: up to 20%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Artillery: no percentage limit
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Artillery: Up to one machine per 800 points
  Allies: Armenian or Maccabean lists
[Later Army 110 AD to 193 AD]
  Characters: up to 20%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Artillery: no percentage limit
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 0%
  Artillery: Up to one machine per 800 points</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
